    {
      "id": "nowinandroid-q3",
      "answer": "Application code is Kotlin with Jetpack Compose/Material 3 and Android ViewModels; coroutines/Flow support reactive state, Hilt supplies dependency injection, Room handles relational storage, Proto DataStore handles preferences, and Retrofit handles remote APIs. XML declares Android components and proto3 defines preferences. Gradle uses Kotlin DSL, an included build-logic build and type-safe project accessors; settings require JDK 17+. Modules separate app, shared core libraries, feature api navigation contracts versus impl UI/logic, sync, tests and benchmarks. Feature impl may depend on other feature api modules; core must not depend on app/features. Demo and prod select local versus backend content.",
