      "id": "nowinandroid-q5",
      "answer": "X lives in feature:bookmarks:impl. BookmarksViewModel.removeFromSavedResources launches work, exposes the undo flag, remembers the removed ID and bookmarks it false. undoBookmarkRemoval writes true for that remembered ID and clears undo state. BookmarksScreen wires remove/undo/clear callbacks; its LaunchedEffect requests the removal snackbar with Undo, invokes undo on a true result, otherwise clears state, and also clears on ON_STOP. BookmarksGrid routes the news-feed bookmark event to removal.",
