      "id": "nowinandroid-q7",
      "answer": "Production call path: BookmarksScreen passes viewModel::removeFromSavedResources; the grid callback supplies the ID. removeFromSavedResources(id) enters viewModelScope.launch and invokes UserDataRepository.setNewsResourceBookmarked(id,false). Hilt DataModule binds that interface to OfflineFirstUserDataRepository, whose suspend override calls NiaPreferencesDataSource.setNewsResourceBookmarked, then logs analytics. The data source calls DataStore.updateData, copies UserPreferences, and removes the ID from bookmarkedNewsResourceIds; IOException is caught/logged. Dispatch boundaries: Compose callback to ViewModel coroutine; interface dispatch resolved by the Hilt binding; DataStore's library-managed update/serialization. The ViewModel launch has no explicit dispatcher, and repository/data-source code has no withContext hop. DataStore is explicitly constructed with applicationScope.coroutineContext + the IO dispatcher, bound to Dispatchers.IO. Serializer.writeTo writes protobuf to the provided output. Library scheduling and generated Hilt internals were not inspected. On the return-data side, preference map keys become UserData bookmarks; CompositeUserNewsResourceRepository.observeAllBookmarked reacts and the ViewModel maps its flow into feed state.",
