      "id": "nowinandroid-q9",
      "answer": "BookmarksViewModelTest manually constructs the real ViewModel using TestUserDataRepository, TestNewsRepository and the real CompositeUserNewsResourceRepository under MainDispatcherRule. oneBookmark_whenRemoving_removesFromFeed seeds a saved resource, collects the feed, calls removeFromSavedResources directly, and checks empty feed plus undo flag. feedUiState_undoneBookmarkRemoval_bookmarkIsRestored removes then calls undoBookmarkRemoval, checking restoration and cleared flag. These exercise ViewModel behavior against an in-memory fake, not production preference persistence. BookmarksScreenTest.feed_whenRemovingBookmark_removesBookmark renders the stateless screen, clicks the matching unbookmark node and verifies its supplied callback/ID; feed_whenLifecycleStops_undoBookmarkedStateIsCleared sends ON_STOP and checks the clear callback. Neither enters the production ViewModel. The related repository test offlineFirstUserDataRepository_bookmark_news_resource_logic_delegates_to_nia_preferences constructs real repository/data source over InMemoryDataStore, but only sets true for two IDs: it does not prove removal/undo or disk persistence. No tests were run, and no end-to-end snackbar-action/persistent undo test was verified.",
