      "id": "nowinandroid-q10",
      "answer": "A concrete UI origin is core:ui newsFeed: onToggleBookmark emits (userNewsResource.id, !isSaved). ForYouScreen routes that pair to ForYouViewModel.updateNewsResourceSaved, which launches UserDataRepository.setNewsResourceBookmarked(id,isChecked); the bookmarks removal/undo path instead forces false/true. The repository API accepts newsResourceId:String and bookmarked:Boolean; its production implementation forwards both unchanged to NiaPreferencesDataSource. In updateData's copied proto, true puts (id,true), while false removes the key entirely. user_preferences.proto field 15 is map<string,bool> bookmarked_news_resource_ids, used as a set; the stored Boolean is merely a set placeholder. DataStoreModule selects user_preferences.pb and UserPreferencesSerializer; writeTo serializes the generated UserPreferences into the output stream. The read side exposes the map's keys as UserData.bookmarkedNewsResources. The ID is not converted or sent through Room for this preference write; generated proto/DataStore disk machinery is an external boundary.",
